<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian government orders truckers to end strike.</title>
<headline>Colombian government orders truckers to end strike.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government on Thursday ordered Colombian truckers to end a five-day strike and said the work stoppage would be declared illegal unless it was called off by midnight.</p>
<p>Leaders of the Colombian Truck Drivers Association (ACC) shrugged off the threat, saying that as private citizens they had no obligation to provide any services to the state.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't have any working relationship with the government,&quot; said Mario Quiroga, the ACC's sectional chief from central Boyaca province and a member of its strike bargaining committee.</p>
</text>
